concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17A After section 15YAB"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-17a ;
    values:originalText "Insert: 15YAC  Child complainants (1) A child complainant, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an offence, of a kind referred to in subsection 15Y(1), to which the proceeding relates (whether or not the child is involved in the proceeding or was involved in the initiation of the proceeding); and  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 (b) includes a person who was such a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed. (2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child complainant if the person informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated as such a complainant. 15YAD  Child witnesses (1) A child witness, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child (including a child complainant) who is a witness in the proceeding; and (b) includes a witness in the proceeding who was a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed. (2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child witness if the person informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated as such a witness." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: 15YAC  Child complainants (1) A child complainant, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an offence, of a kind referred to in subsection 15Y(1), to which the proceeding relates (whether or not the child is involved in the proceeding or was involved in the initiation of the proceeding); and  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 (b) includes a person who was such a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed. (2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child complainant if the person informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated as such a complainant. 15YAD  Child witnesses (1) A child witness, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child (including a child complainant) who is a witness in the proceeding; and (b) includes a witness in the proceeding who was a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed. (2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child witness if the person informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated as such a witness."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c1a9e807ecf33ae8eb7949f09ca5b504308ef5af48cd54588c4c1469a734000f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.10" .
doc:sch-1-sec-17a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "17A After section 15YAB" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Insert: 15YAC  Child complainants (1) A child complainant, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an offence, of a kind referred to in subsection 15Y(1), to which the proceeding relates (whether or not the child is involved in the proceeding or was involved in the initiation of the proceeding); and  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 (b) includes a person who was such a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed. (2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child complainant if the person informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated as such a complainant. 15YAD  Child witnesses (1) A child witness, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child (including a child complainant) who is a witness in the proceeding; and (b) includes a witness in the proceeding who was a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed. (2) However, a person who is 18 or over is not a child witness if the person informs the court that the person does not wish to be treated as such a witness." ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17A(1) After section 15YAB"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-17a-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A child complainant, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an offence, of a kind referred to in subsection 15Y(1), to which the proceeding relates (whether or not the child is involved in the proceeding or was involved in the initiation of the proceeding); and  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 (b) includes a person who was such a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A child complainant, in relation to a child proceeding: (a) is a child who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an offence, of a kind referred to in subsection 15Y(1), to which the proceeding relates (whether or not the child is involved in the proceeding or was involved in the initiation of the proceeding); and  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 (b) includes a person who was such a child at the time the offence concerned was alleged to have been committed."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9ec38e1aef7e97bb22872370c8dffb0b3f386c45c45d4ff69b4497fca8e1b2e0" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-17a ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines a child witness in relation to a child proceeding. A child complainant in a child proceeding is defined as a child who is or was involved in the initiation of the proceeding." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
