concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32 At the end of Division 4 of Part IAD"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-32 ;
    values:originalText "Add: 15YLA  Recording of evidence given in person (1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to whom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if: (a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in another proceeding; and (b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and (c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.  Schedule 1  Amendments  Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 No. 114, 2024 (2) This subsection applies to the following persons: (a) for a child proceeding—a child witness; (b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult complainant; (c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom an order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this section. (3) The recording may be a video or audio recording. (4) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the evidence is given by closed-circuit television." ;
    skos:definition "Add: 15YLA  Recording of evidence given in person (1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to whom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if: (a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in another proceeding; and (b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and (c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.  Schedule 1  Amendments  Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 No. 114, 2024 (2) This subsection applies to the following persons: (a) for a child proceeding—a child witness; (b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult complainant; (c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom an order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this section. (3) The recording may be a video or audio recording. (4) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the evidence is given by closed-circuit television."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a660dfca8e7e23a7192aaeb1a3be7d8c11579143eec7fe769bc8dccd0b7f721c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-32-ss-1 ;
