concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-37 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37 At the end of section 15YM"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-37 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 Offence (5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage or alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and (b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both. (6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 Offence (5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage or alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and (b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both. (6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e3fff83a71d8782baf84fd98a8b3581809eadafedf93968655501c75c01025fd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-37-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-37-ss-6 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024.pdf, p.20" .
doc:sch-1-sec-37 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "37 At the end of section 15YM" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Add:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 114, 2024 Crimes Amendment (Strengthening the Criminal Justice Response to Sexual Violence) Act 2024 Offence (5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage or alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and (b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both. (6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention." ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-amendment-strengthening-the-criminal-justice-response-to-sexual-violence-act-2024-sch-1-sec-37-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37(5) At the end of section 15YM"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-37-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage or alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and (b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both." ;
    skos:definition "(5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage or alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or (iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and (b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "78784ba1b5936a4f34049e3ecc8f2dcedd880c37cf233642da912b8517629ee2" ;
